  "observation": "The compiled decoder reproduces all 27 retained original returns and 374216 bytes for fields 23/14/15 and parses the exact captured event/collision records. Compiled initialization reproduces 25 original actor defaults, 25 RNG steps and 50 floor queries with 686400 exact captured payload bytes. The C++ battle-request handler reproduces six original calls and all thirteen complete boundaries (4516 range bytes,4512 distinct bytes each), five pending retries and immediate-zero acceptance.",
  "interpretation": "Stable required loading/initialization/request behavior now exists in the existing C++ library. Event packages expose EventProgram, initialization uses parsed collision layers, and defaults/snapshot restore share one original-to-event projection. Original table and byte accesses remain explicit; source-derived unobserved branches remain separate from the recorded execution scope.",
